  "title": "India's Retail Inflation and Trade Deficit Amid Global Challenges",
  "summary": "India's retail inflation rose to 4.45% in July, driven by higher food prices, while economists expect no immediate rate hike despite rising upside risks. India's trade deficit widened to $31.98 billion in Q1FY27, partially offset by growth in exports of petroleum products, electronics, engineering, and marine goods. India's inflation likely rose to 5.4% in September due to increased food and crude oil prices. The Eurozone's inflation hit a three-year high of 3.8%, and UK inflation accelerated to 2.9% amid energy price shocks and rising oil prices.",
